   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The 747-8's sheets are low-resolution binarized scans with the sheet's grid drawn through the aircraft, too coarse to trace as the other shapes are: so the shape is the 747-400F's measured outlines (shapes/B744.json, from D6-58326-1) with the 747-8's two fuselage plugs, 4.10 m ahead of the wing and 1.49 m behind it (the door table 2.7.1 puts doors 2 and 3 4.1 m, doors 4 and 5 5.6 m further back than the 747-400's; 74.22 m nose to tail cone), and its new wing (raked tips), GEnx-2B nacelles and their positions read off the scans (tools/trace/b748/derive.py) to about 0.1 m. The fin and tailplane are the 747-400's, moved back with the plugs (the sheet prints the tailplane 21.99 m across, the 747-400's 22.17 m). Doors as the 747-400F's, moved with the plugs, but for the main-deck cargo door, where the scan draws it (its middle at the printed 48.26 m), and the one passenger door (the forward one). Confidence medium for the scans."
  }
